<tr>
                        <td colspan="10">KVPTG/GPWIS/L3/G9C(31775,31637,31768/WATE] JDB A/04.15HRS SIGNAL TAKEN OFF A/5.01 HRS ,AT 05.05 HRS LP INFORMED ABOUT LOCO TROUBLE , TLC REPORTED THAT LOCO AXLE LOCKED.AND NOT RECTIFIED MADE TR AT 11.40 HRS AND SAME WAS STABLED AT JDB
Dept Remarks: T.NO KVPTG/GPWIS3/G9 . TRAIN DEP KMEZ AT 04.22HRS ,KMEZ SM INFORMED SMOKE COMING
FROM BOGIE 1, TRAIN JDB A/ 04.43HRS ON THOROUGH CHECKING FOUND SMOKE COMING FROM WHEEL
NO 3 AND C. L.I JDB ATTENDED AT 05.25 HRS AND SUSPECTED HWEEL NO3 LOCKED AXEL SA</td>
                       <td colspan="6"></td>
</tr>
<tr>
                                                <td style="font-weight: bold; color: black;">21.</td>
                                                <td style="font-weight: bold; color: black;">TLC Remarks:</td>


</tr>
<tr>
                        <td colspan="10">LP Mobile No: 9752498043. 20:15 Crew TO at BCHL and CTO at R/6. 20:45 Train Dep BCHL. 04:22 Train Dep KMEZ on through signal. While on Run SM/KMEZ informed to LP through Walkie-Talkie that smoke emission from Bogie-1 of Middle Loco(31637/WAG-9/WATE). 04:43 Train arrival JDB R/2. 04:53 LP FIR from JDB that, at JDB checked Middle Loco (31637/WAG-9/WATE) as per the information of SM/KMEZ found slight smoke emission. 05:00 TLC advised CLI JDB to attend the same. 05:25 Sri R.BISOI CLI/JDB attended and informed that Wheel No-3 not moving suspected Locked Axle. 05:30 Advised maintenance staff KRPU to proceed by first available train to JDB, also informed to PPO/ELS VSKP over Phone to attend the same. 08:55 KRPU maintenance staff dep by 18107 to JDB to attend the same. On Date 08.06.2026: 04:45 - Outgoing crew T.O at JDB LP: PANKAJ KUMAR/KRPU ALP: C G H K REDDY/KRP 07:10 HRS(08.06.2026) As per SSE/ELS/VSKP give fit memo at JDB/SS 07:10 Hrs for normal speed towards home shed for one trip. 08:49 - Train departed from JDB</td>
                        <td colspan="6"></td>
</tr>
<tr>
                                                <td style="font-weight: bold; color: black;">22.</td>
                                                <td colspan="3" style="font-weight: bold; color: black;">Shed Report After Investigation:</td>
</tr>
<tr>
                          <td colspan="10">failed loco is 31637:
On 08.06.26 Pinion cut at JDB due to TM-3 Outer labyrinth/deflector ring came out and TM seized.
Loco arrived ELS VSKP on 10/06/2026 at 05:45 hrs, where it was lifted and TM3 was removed on 10-06-2026. Dismantling of TM3 was carried out on 11-06-2026, and the following observations were made:
1.        The outer labyrinth came out, severely scoring the rotor shaft and rubbing against the bull gear, which formed a groove on the labyrinth.
2.        Gear case oil entered the DE end bearing housing and contaminated the bearing grease
3.         DE end bearing rollers are badly rubbed and have formed a step pattern.
4.        Rotor rubbing against the stator core.
CONCLUSION: The outer labyrinth shifted out of position due to improper fitment and an inadequate interference fit on the rotor shaft. Displaced loose labyrinth, scoring the rotating shaft and rubbing against the bull gear to form a groove. Gearcase oil has leaked through the displaced labyrinth seal gap and has entered the DE end bearing housing. The penetrating gear case oil thinned and washed out the existing bearing grease. Starvation of grease caused rapid frictional heating, which damaged the cage ring and displaced the rollers, leading to a bearing seizure and ultimately a traction motor failure.
NOTE: 
VCU data downlaoded and found no any abnormal messages are logged at the time of failure . SR1&amp;2 data downloaded and observed "Over temperature Motor3 " only logged.
TM 3 DETAILS: 
TM NO. 13229, MAKE CLW, 
ROTOR NO. CLW RTG S 4470, MAKE CLW
RECD ALONG WITH LOCO  32980 TM5 ON 10-12-2020 FROM CLW, 
D.O.C - 31-12-2020
LAST OH ON 19-05-2026 BY BANITHA, FITTED IN LOCO 31637 AS TM3 ON 02-06-2026 DURING TOH

LAST GREASE SAMPLE CHECKED DURING OH, DE - 94 PPM, NDE - 120 PPM
Bearing : M/s FAG,
Labyrinth: M/s NEPL ( NARAMADA Enterprises PVT.LTD),
Pinion: M/s GGAG (21 teeth).</td>
                          <td colspan="6"></td>
</tr>
<tr>
