Loco arrived ELS VSKP on 10/06/2026 at 05:45 hrs, where it was lifted and TM3 was removed on 10-06-2026. Dismantling of TM3 was carried out on 11-06-2026,
CONCLUSION: The outer labyrinth shifted out of position due to improper fitment and an inadequate interference fit on the rotor shaft. Displaced loose labyrinth, scoring the rotating shaft and rubbing against the bull gear to form a groove. Gearcase oil has leaked through the displaced labyrinth seal gap and has entered the DE end bearing housing. The penetrating gear case oil thinned and washed out the existing bearing grease. Starvation of grease caused rapid frictional heating, which damaged the cage ring and displaced the rollers, leading to a bearing seizure and ultimately a traction motor failure.
NOTE: 
VCU data downloaded and found no any abnormal messages are logged at the time of failure. SR1&amp;2 data downloaded and observed "Over temperature Motor3 " only logged.</td>
